<file path="README.md">
# Dara-Manihot Industries & Farms

Marketing site for Dara-Manihot Industries & Farms: sustainable agriculture,
renewable energy, biomass gasification and green hydrogen in Nigeria.

**Stack:** Next.js 16 (App Router, Turbopack) · React 19 · Tailwind CSS 4 ·
shadcn/ui + Radix · Motion · TypeScript · Biome + ESLint · Vitest + Playwright.

## Getting started

Requires Node.js **20.9+** (a Next.js 16 requirement).

```bash
pnpm install
pnpm dev            # http://localhost:3000
```

| Script | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `pnpm dev` / `build` / `start` | Next.js dev server, production build, serve the build |
| `pnpm lint` | ESLint (Next 16 removed `next lint`, so this is the plain ESLint CLI) |
| `pnpm format` | Biome: format + organise imports + safe fixes |
| `pnpm typecheck` | Generates typed-route definitions, then `tsc --noEmit` |
| `pnpm test` | Unit/component tests (Vitest + Testing Library) |
| `pnpm test:e2e` | Browser tests (Playwright). Needs a build first; first run: `pnpm exec playwright install chromium` |
| `pnpm check` | lint + typecheck + unit tests |
| `pnpm launch:check` | Lists everything still blocking a production launch (missing email settings, placeholder team, photos). Exits 1 on blockers |
| `pnpm webmail:provision` | Creates the five business mailboxes through cPanel. Dry run unless given `-- --apply`. See `docs/EMAIL-SETUP.md` |

> Next 16 no longer lints during `next build`. Run `pnpm check` in CI.

## Environment

The enquiry form uses ZeptoMail API for both company notifications and visitor acknowledgements. Set `MAIL_DRIVER=zeptomail`, `ZEPTOMAIL_TOKEN`, and a complete authorised `ZEPTOMAIL_FROM_EMAIL`; `ENQUIRY_TO` defaults to `daramanihot@gmail.com,info@daramanihot.com`. Legacy SMTP remains available with `MAIL_DRIVER=smtp`. Copy `.env.example` to
`.env.local` and fill it in; production sets the same variables in the host's
environment. Without them the form shows a friendly error and nothing is lost
silently. Full guide: [`docs/EMAIL-SETUP.md`](docs/EMAIL-SETUP.md).

## Project structure

```
app/
  layout.tsx            fonts, metadata, header/footer, skip link, back-to-top
  globals.css           ALL design tokens (see below)
  page.tsx              home
  (pages)/              about, services, projects, contact, privacy, terms
  fonts/                self-hosted Young Serif + Figtree (woff2)
components/
  ui/                   shadcn/ui primitives (button, badge, card, sheet, navigation-menu, separator)
  sections/             page-level building blocks (home-hero, page-hero, section-heading, cta-band, legal-document)
  site-header.tsx       sticky header + desktop navigation
  mobile-nav.tsx        right-hand app drawer (bounce in/out)
  hero-carousel.tsx     background image carousel
  back-to-top.tsx, copy-button.tsx, animations.tsx, footer.tsx, logo.tsx
lib/
  constants.ts          company info, nav, hero slides: the single source of truth
  services.ts, legal.ts content for the services and the Privacy/Terms pages
tests/                  unit + component tests
e2e/                    Playwright tests
public/                 logo.png, hero images, humans.txt
```

## Design tokens

Everything visual is defined in **`app/globals.css`**; components never use a
raw colour. A test (`tests/design-tokens.test.ts`) fails the build if a
component uses a Tailwind palette class (`bg-green-600`) or a hex/rgb value.

* **Palette** is sampled from the logo: leaf green (`--primary`) and wordmark
  purple (`--secondary`).
* **Every call-to-action is the secondary colour**: use
  `<Button variant="cta">`. To re-colour all CTAs, change `--secondary`
  (and `--secondary-hover`).
* **Gradients and overlays**: the home carousel has no gradient (legibility
  comes from `text-on-photo`, a token text shadow). `--band-gradient` and
  `--page-hero-gradient` (the Contact page hero) are solid brand gradients;
  `--page-hero-overlay` is the translucent green laid over a hero photo
  (`PageHero image=...`, photos listed in `PAGE_HERO_IMAGES` in
  `lib/constants.ts`). A test enforces AA contrast for the overlay.
* **Type**: `font-display` (Young Serif, headings) and `font-sans` (Figtree).
  Fluid sizes: `text-display`, `text-title`, `text-lead`.
* **Layout**: `--header-h`, `--container-max`, `--section-y`; utilities
  `page-container`, `section-y`, `scroll-mt-header`.
* **Motion**: `--ease-bounce`, drawer and hero durations, keyframes. Contrast
  of the key colour pairs is asserted at WCAG AA in the token test.

## Common tasks

**Replace the hero images.** Put your photos in `public/images/hero/` and edit
`HERO_SLIDES` in `lib/constants.ts` (path, alt text, caption, and an optional
`position` to tune the crop). Keep the subject near the horizontal centre:
phones show only the middle third. The four images shipped are placeholder
illustrations.

**Add the client's photos.** Every image on the site is a named slot in
`lib/imagery.ts`. Drop a file in `public/images/`, set the slot's `src` and
`alt`. The full shot list for the client is in
[`docs/PHOTO-REQUEST.md`](docs/PHOTO-REQUEST.md).

**Add or change a service.** Edit `SERVICES` in `lib/services.ts` and give it a
`pillar` (`sustainable-agriculture`, `sustainable-energy` or `supporting`). It
then appears in the right Services section, the enquiry form's service list
and the footer, with no other change.

**Replace the placeholder team.** Edit `lib/team.ts`, set `placeholder: false`.

**Update contact details.** Edit `COMPANY_INFO` in `lib/constants.ts`. The
header, footer, contact page and legal pages all read from it.

**Cookie consent.** `lib/cookie-consent.ts` stores the choice (localStorage, 12
months, versioned; no cookie is set), `hooks/use-cookie-consent.ts` reads it,
`CookieBanner` asks, and the footer's "Cookie settings" reopens it. Only the
Contact page Google map is gated: `OfficeMap` loads it automatically once the
visitor accepts. To gate something new, read `useCookieConsent().state ===
'accepted'`, and bump `CONSENT_VERSION` plus the Privacy Policy when accepting
starts to cover more.

**Update legal text.** Edit `lib/legal.ts` and bump `LEGAL_LAST_UPDATED` in
`lib/constants.ts`.

**Add a page.** Create `app/(pages)/<name>/page.tsx` with a `metadata` export,
add it to `NAVIGATION_LINKS`, and (for the mobile drawer) an icon in
`components/mobile-nav.tsx`. TypeScript flags the missing icon, and
`typedRoutes` flags any link to a route that doesn't exist.

## Accessibility and motion

Skip link, visible focus rings, `aria-current` on the active page, a focus-
trapped dialog for the drawer, a pause button on the carousel, and
`prefers-reduced-motion` support everywhere (no autoplay, no push-in, no
bounce). Scroll reveals fall back to visible content when JS is off.

### The Appear effect

Everything that fades in on scroll uses one effect, from `components/animations.tsx`:
`Reveal` (fade and lift once, when scrolled into view), `Stagger` and
`StaggerList` (children appear one after another) and `FadeIn` (fade only, for a
picture that fills its box). The old scroll-linked `ScrollFade` is gone. The
closing call to action fades its photo in first (`CTA_IMAGE_DURATION`), then
its words (`CTA_CONTENT_DELAY`); both live in `lib/motion.ts`.

### Cookie preferences

The banner (`components/cookie-banner.tsx`) has two switches. **Essential** is
always on and locked. **Non-essential** is off by default and covers the Google
map on the Contact page. Turning it on opens "Why does the map need cookies?",
which explains that Google receives the visitor's IP address and may set
cookies. The stored choice stays binary (`accepted` or `declined`) in
`lib/cookie-consent.ts`: "Accept all" and "Save choices" with the switch on store
`accepted`; "Reject non-essential" and "Save choices" with it off store
`declined`. If you add a second non-essential category, extend the stored shape
and bump `CONSENT_VERSION` so everyone is asked again.

### Colour notes

Icons and their round chips use the secondary purple: `bg-secondary-soft
text-secondary` for a chip, `text-secondary` for a bare icon. Inner page banners
with a photo get the translucent green `bg-page-hero-overlay`. Fields on the dark
enquiry card (`surface-canopy`) are a translucent lighter green with a light
outline.


Organisation notifications now address both `daramanihot@gmail.com` and `info@daramanihot.com` in one email. `ENQUIRY_TO` accepts a comma-separated list, trims whitespace, rejects malformed/empty entries and removes duplicates. The visitor receives a separate acknowledgement, with both organisation inboxes as Reply-To. The sender and public domain/email content are unchanged. Update the Vercel `ENQUIRY_TO` setting to `daramanihot@gmail.com,info@daramanihot.com` and redeploy; an old explicit environment value overrides code defaults. No live emails are sent by tests.
</file>

<file path="app/globals.css">
@import "tailwindcss";
@import "tw-animate-css";

@custom-variant dark (&:is(.dark *));

/* ==========================================================================
   DESIGN TOKENS
   Every colour, size, radius, shadow and timing used by the site is defined
   here. Components reference semantic tokens (bg-primary, text-secondary,
   --header-h ...) and never hard-code a hex value or a raw palette colour.

   1. Brand palette   raw values, sampled from the Dara-Manihot logo
   2. Semantic tokens what components use (shadcn naming + a few additions)
   3. Layout / motion non-colour tokens
   4. @theme          exposes the tokens as Tailwind utilities
   5. Base, utilities and keyframes
   ========================================================================== */

/* 1 + 2 + 3 ---------------------------------------------------------------- */
:root {
  /* Brand palette. Green = the leaf, purple = the wordmark. */
  --brand-green-950: #08280d;
  --brand-green-900: #0d3a16;
  --brand-green-800: #11501d;
  --brand-green-700: #176827;
  --brand-green-600: #1f7f31;
  --brand-green-200: #c7e4cb;
  --brand-green-100: #e1f1e4;
  --brand-green-50: #f1f8f2;
  --brand-purple-900: #46094f;
  --brand-purple-700: #6c1b7d;
  --brand-purple-600: #84289a;
  --brand-purple-300: #d7a8e4;
  --brand-purple-100: #f3e6f7;
  --brand-ink: #16211a;
  --brand-ivory: #fbfcfa;
  --brand-mist: #f0f5ee;
  --brand-line: #d9e3d8;
  --brand-slate: #4f5f54;
  --brand-white: #ffffff;
  --brand-danger: #b42318;
  --brand-danger-light: #ffb4ab;

  /* Semantic tokens (light) */
  --background: var(--brand-ivory);
  --foreground: var(--brand-ink);
  --card: var(--brand-white);
  --card-foreground: var(--brand-ink);
  --popover: var(--brand-white);
  --popover-foreground: var(--brand-ink);
  --primary: var(--brand-green-700);
  --primary-foreground: var(--brand-white);
  /* Secondary = the CTA colour. Every call-to-action button uses it. */
  --secondary: var(--brand-purple-600);
  --secondary-foreground: var(--brand-white);
  --secondary-hover: var(--brand-purple-700);
  /* Pale purple: the round chip behind a purple icon. */
  --secondary-soft: var(--brand-purple-100);
  --leaf: var(--brand-green-600);
  --leaf-foreground: var(--brand-white);
  --leaf-hover: var(--brand-green-700);
  --muted: var(--brand-mist);
  --muted-foreground: var(--brand-slate);
  --accent: var(--brand-green-100);
  --accent-foreground: var(--brand-green-900);
  --destructive: var(--brand-danger);
  --border: var(--brand-line);
  --input: var(--brand-line);
  --ring: var(--brand-green-600);

  /* Deep brand surfaces: hero overlay, CTA bands, footer */
  --canopy: var(--brand-green-950);
  --canopy-foreground: var(--brand-white);
  --canopy-muted: var(--brand-green-200);

  /* Mint: the pale green that tints whole sections (Who we are, Strategic
     partnerships) and the tiles on them. Dark text stays AA on it. */
  --mint: var(--brand-green-200);

  /* Chart + sidebar tokens kept for shadcn compatibility */
  --chart-1: var(--brand-green-700);
  --chart-2: var(--brand-purple-600);
  --chart-3: var(--brand-green-600);
  --chart-4: var(--brand-purple-300);
  --chart-5: var(--brand-green-200);
  --sidebar: var(--brand-mist);
  --sidebar-foreground: var(--brand-ink);
  --sidebar-primary: var(--brand-green-700);
  --sidebar-primary-foreground: var(--brand-white);
  --sidebar-accent: var(--brand-green-100);
  --sidebar-accent-foreground: var(--brand-green-900);
  --sidebar-border: var(--brand-line);
  --sidebar-ring: var(--brand-green-600);

  /* Gradients: the site colour (green) laid over photography and bands */
  --hero-gradient: linear-gradient(
    100deg,
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-green-950) 94%, transparent) 0%,
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-green-900) 78%, transparent) 38%,
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-green-800) 28%, transparent) 72%,
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-green-800) 8%, transparent) 100%
  );
  --hero-gradient-bottom: linear-gradient(
    0deg,
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-green-950) 88%, transparent) 0%,
    transparent 38%
  );

  /* Inner page banners with a photo: the same green as --page-hero-gradient,
   but translucent so the picture shows through. Keep every stop at 82% or
   above: that is what keeps white text AA over even a pure white photo
   (tests/design-tokens.test.ts asserts it). */
  --page-hero-overlay: linear-gradient(
    115deg,
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-green-950) 94%, transparent) 0%,
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-green-900) 88%, transparent) 55%,
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-green-800) 82%, transparent) 100%
  );
  /* Legibility for text set directly on a bare photograph (landing hero),
     where no colour is laid over the picture. */
  --text-on-photo-shadow:
    0 1px 2px color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-green-950) 60%, transparent),
    0 2px 24px color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-green-950) 50%, transparent);

  --band-gradient: linear-gradient(
    120deg,
    var(--brand-green-950) 0%,
    var(--brand-green-800) 70%,
    var(--brand-green-700) 100%
  );
  --page-hero-gradient: linear-gradient(
    115deg,
    var(--brand-green-950) 0%,
    var(--brand-green-900) 55%,
    var(--brand-green-800) 100%
  );
  /* Photo band (landing page CTA): a deep-green veil so white text reads
     over any photograph. */
  --image-band-overlay: linear-gradient(
    180deg,
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-green-950) 78%, transparent) 0%,
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-green-950) 66%, transparent) 55%,
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-green-900) 80%, transparent) 100%
  );

  /* Frosted glass (navbar). A white tint that lets the page show through,
     with a brighter top edge like light catching real glass. */
  --glass-tint: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-white) 54%, transparent);
  --glass-tint-scrolled: color-mix(
    in srgb,
    var(--brand-white) 72%,
    transparent
  );
  --glass-highlight: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-white) 85%, transparent);
  --glass-edge: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-ink) 14%, transparent);
  --glass-blur: 22px;

  /* Shape + depth */
  --radius: 0.75rem;
  --shadow-lift: 0 18px 36px -18px
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-green-950) 45%, transparent);
  --shadow-float: 0 10px 28px -8px
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-green-950) 55%, transparent);

  /* Layout */
  --header-top: 1rem;
  --header-h: 5.25rem;
  --hero-pad: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 6rem);
  --container-max: 76rem;
  --container-pad: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 2rem);
  --section-y: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
  /* Mobile menu: a floating glass panel that grows out of the hamburger.
     The origin is the hamburger's centre, measured from the panel's top-right
     corner: 1.875rem in from the right edge (pill padding + half the button)
     and 2.375rem above the panel's top (the panel sits at --header-h). */
  --menu-w: min(92vw, 22rem);
  --menu-origin: calc(100% - 1.875rem) calc(2.875rem - var(--header-h));

  /* Motion */
  --ease-bounce: cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1);
  --ease-out-expo: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  --hero-interval: 6500ms;
  --hero-fade: 1100ms;
}

/* On narrow screens the photo is cropped to its middle, so a left-to-right
   gradient would bury it. Use a top-to-bottom wash instead. */
@media (max-width: 47.99rem) {
  :root {
    --hero-gradient: linear-gradient(
      100deg,
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-green-950) 62%, transparent) 0%,
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-green-900) 40%, transparent) 38%,
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-green-800) 10%, transparent) 70%,
      transparent 100%
    );
  }
}

/* Dark-mode overrides. No toggle ships yet; the tokens keep one a drop-in. */
.dark {
  --background: #0c1710;
  --foreground: #eef4ee;
  --card: #122019;
  --card-foreground: #eef4ee;
  --popover: #122019;
  --popover-foreground: #eef4ee;
  --primary: #3aa74e;
  --primary-foreground: #08280d;
  --secondary: #a24bb8;
  --secondary-foreground: #ffffff;
  --secondary-hover: #b560c9;
  --secondary-soft: #2a1730;
  --muted: #16271c;
  --muted-foreground: #a9b9ad;
  --accent: #1a3323;
  --accent-foreground: #e1f1e4;
  --border: #25382b;
  --input: #25382b;
  --ring: #3aa74e;
}

/* 4. Tailwind theme ------------------------------------------------------- */
@theme inline {
  --color-background: var(--background);
  --color-foreground: var(--foreground);
  --color-card: var(--card);
  --color-card-foreground: var(--card-foreground);
  --color-popover: var(--popover);
  --color-popover-foreground: var(--popover-foreground);
  --color-primary: var(--primary);
  --color-primary-foreground: var(--primary-foreground);
  --color-secondary: var(--secondary);
  --color-secondary-foreground: var(--secondary-foreground);
  --color-secondary-hover: var(--secondary-hover);
  --color-secondary-soft: var(--secondary-soft);
  --color-muted: var(--muted);
  --color-muted-foreground: var(--muted-foreground);
  --color-accent: var(--accent);
  --color-accent-foreground: var(--accent-foreground);
  --color-destructive: var(--destructive);
  --color-border: var(--border);
  --color-input: var(--input);
  --color-ring: var(--ring);
  --color-canopy: var(--canopy);
  --color-canopy-foreground: var(--canopy-foreground);
  --color-canopy-muted: var(--canopy-muted);
  --color-mint: var(--mint);
  --color-chart-1: var(--chart-1);
  --color-chart-2: var(--chart-2);
  --color-chart-3: var(--chart-3);
  --color-chart-4: var(--chart-4);
  --color-chart-5: var(--chart-5);
  --color-sidebar: var(--sidebar);
  --color-sidebar-foreground: var(--sidebar-foreground);
  --color-sidebar-primary: var(--sidebar-primary);
  --color-sidebar-primary-foreground: var(--sidebar-primary-foreground);
  --color-sidebar-accent: var(--sidebar-accent);
  --color-sidebar-accent-foreground: var(--sidebar-accent-foreground);
  --color-sidebar-border: var(--sidebar-border);
  --color-sidebar-ring: var(--sidebar-ring);
  --color-leaf: var(--leaf);
  --color-leaf-foreground: var(--leaf-foreground);
  --color-leaf-hover: var(--leaf-hover);
  --text-hero: clamp(2.25rem, 1.5rem + 1.95vw, 3.25rem);
  --text-hero--line-height: 1.25;

  --font-sans: var(--font-figtree), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
  --font-display: var(--font-young-serif), ui-serif, Georgia, serif;

  --radius-sm: calc(var(--radius) - 4px);
  --radius-md: calc(var(--radius) - 2px);
  --radius-lg: var(--radius);
  --radius-xl: calc(var(--radius) + 4px);
  --radius-2xl: calc(var(--radius) + 10px);

  --shadow-lift: var(--shadow-lift);
  --shadow-float: var(--shadow-float);

  --ease-bounce: var(--ease-bounce);
  --ease-out-expo: var(--ease-out-expo);

  /* Fluid type scale */
  --text-display: clamp(2.25rem, 1.35rem + 3.4vw, 4.25rem);
  --text-display--line-height: 1.04;
  --text-display--letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  --text-title: clamp(1.875rem, 1.35rem + 2.1vw, 3rem);
  --text-title--line-height: 1.12;
  --text-title--letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  --text-lead: clamp(1.125rem, 1.02rem + 0.45vw, 1.375rem);
  --text-lead--line-height: 1.6;
  /* Large centred pull-statement (the vision). */
  --text-statement: clamp(1.625rem, 1.05rem + 2.1vw, 2.75rem);
  --text-statement--line-height: 1.28;
  /* The "Who we are" company statement: large, set in semibold. */
  --text-intro: clamp(1.375rem, 1.05rem + 1vw, 1.875rem);
  --text-intro--line-height: 1.4;
}

/* Animation tokens + keyframes. Kept outside `inline` so they stay var-based. */
@theme {
  --animate-rise: rise 760ms var(--ease-out-expo) both;
  --animate-hero-progress: hero-progress var(--hero-interval) linear forwards;

  @keyframes rise {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(1.25rem);
    }
    to {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0);
    }
  }
  @keyframes hero-progress {
    from {
      transform: scaleX(0);
    }
    to {
      transform: scaleX(1);
    }
  }
}

/* 5. Base ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
@layer base {
  * {
    @apply border-border outline-ring/50;
  }
  html {
    -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
  }
  body {
    @apply bg-background font-sans text-foreground antialiased;
  }
  h1,
  h2,
  h3,
  h4 {
    @apply font-display font-normal text-balance;
  }
  p {
    @apply text-pretty;
  }
  /* Display faces ship a single weight: stop browsers faking a bold. */
  h1,
  h2,
  h3,
  h4,
  .font-display {
    font-synthesis: none;
  }
  ::selection {
    background: var(--brand-purple-300);
    color: var(--brand-green-950);
  }
}

/* Utilities ---------------------------------------------------------------- */
@utility page-container {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: var(--container-max);
  margin-inline: auto;
  padding-inline: var(--container-pad);
}

@utility section-y {
  padding-block: var(--section-y);
}

@utility scroll-mt-header {
  scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--header-h) + 1.25rem);
}

@utility bg-hero-gradient {
  background-image: var(--hero-gradient);
}

@utility bg-hero-gradient-bottom {
  background-image: var(--hero-gradient-bottom);
}

@utility bg-band-gradient {
  background-image: var(--band-gradient);
}

@utility bg-page-hero-gradient {
  background-image: var(--page-hero-gradient);
}

@utility bg-image-band-overlay {
  background-image: var(--image-band-overlay);
}

/* Translucent green veil over an inner page's banner photo. Without this
   utility the class was a silent no-op and the photo had no gradient. */
@utility bg-page-hero-overlay {
  background-image: var(--page-hero-overlay);
}

/* Legibility shadow for text set directly on a bare photograph. */
@utility text-on-photo {
  text-shadow: var(--text-on-photo-shadow);
}

/* Frosted glass surface: blur + saturation lift over a translucent tint, a
   bright inner top edge and a hairline outline. `data-scrolled="true"` on the
   element firms the tint up so text stays legible over busy photography.
   Browsers without backdrop-filter get a near-opaque tint instead of an
   unreadable see-through bar. */
@utility glass {
  background-color: var(--glass-tint);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur)) saturate(1.6);
  backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur)) saturate(1.6);
  box-shadow:
    inset 0 1px 0 var(--glass-highlight),
    inset 0 0 0 1px var(--glass-edge),
    var(--shadow-float);
  &[data-scrolled="true"] {
    background-color: var(--glass-tint-scrolled);
  }
  @supports not (
      (backdrop-filter: blur(1px)) or
      (-webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(1px))
    ) {
    background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-white) 94%, transparent);
  }
}

/* A dark (canopy) surface that hosts the normal light-theme form controls.
   Re-points the semantic tokens for everything inside it, so Input, Select,
   Textarea, labels, hints, errors and links restyle without any component
   knowing about the surface. Fields become a lighter, translucent green fill
   with a light outline. */
@utility surface-canopy {
  --foreground: var(--canopy-foreground);
  --muted-foreground: var(--canopy-muted);
  --background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--canopy-muted) 16%, transparent);
  --input: color-mix(in srgb, var(--canopy-foreground) 45%, transparent);
  --ring: var(--canopy-foreground);
  --destructive: var(--brand-danger-light);
  & [data-slot="input"],
  & [data-slot="select"],
  & [data-slot="textarea"] {
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
  }
  /* Native option lists are drawn by the OS: keep them light and legible. */
  & :is(option, optgroup) {
    background-color: var(--brand-white);
    color: var(--brand-ink);
  }
}

/* Placeholder behind the office map before it is loaded: a faint street grid
   in the logo green, so the panel reads as a map without loading one. */
@utility bg-map-grid {
  background-image:
    linear-gradient(
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary) 14%, transparent) 1px,
      transparent 1px
    ),
    linear-gradient(
      90deg,
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary) 14%, transparent) 1px,
      transparent 1px
    );
  background-size: 2.5rem 2.5rem;
}

/* Staggered entrance delay for the hero's CSS-only load-in sequence. */
@utility animation-delay-* {
  animation-delay: calc(--value(integer) * 1ms);
}

/* Hero carousel: crossfade + slow push-in. Both are driven by the
   `data-active` attribute so there is no JS animation loop. */
@utility hero-slide {
  opacity: 0;
  transform: scale(1);
  transition:
    opacity var(--hero-fade) ease-in-out,
    transform 0s linear var(--hero-fade);
  &[data-active="true"] {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: scale(1.07);
    transition:
      opacity var(--hero-fade) ease-in-out,
      transform calc(var(--hero-interval) + var(--hero-fade)) linear;
  }
}

/* Reduced motion: no push-in, no entrance rise, no autoplay progress. */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .hero-slide[data-active="true"] {
    transform: scale(1);
    transition: opacity 200ms linear;
  }
  .hero-slide {
    transition: opacity 200ms linear;
  }
}
</file>

